hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3009","Asim bin Umar bin Qatadah Ansari reported that Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Umar bin Al Khattab (RA) searched for the heir of Ibn al-Dahdaha, but he did not find them, so he gave the property of Ibn al-Dahdaha to his maternal uncles."
"3010","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Allah and the Messenger are the guardians of the one who has no guardian, and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir."
"3011","Ziyad said: When the case of maternal uncle and aunt was brought to Sayyiduna Umar, he gave two-thirds to the maternal uncle and one-third to the aunt."
"3012","On the authority of Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, gave one-third to his aunt and two-thirds to his maternal grandmother."
"3013","Qays bin Habtar Nahshli said: When the issue of aunt and paternal grandmother was brought to Abdul Malik bin Marwan, a sheikh stood up and said: I was present with Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he gave a third to the aunt and two thirds to the paternal grandmother. And they intended to write it down, then said: Where will Zayed go from this?"
"3014","On the authority of Masrooq, may God have mercy on him: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: An aunt is in the rank of a mother, and an aunt is in the rank of a father, and a niece is in the rank of a brother, and every relative is in the rank of a close relative of the deceased who is not a close heir."
"3015","Dahhak bin Qays narrated that Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) decided about inheritance in the plague of Ummwas (or the first plague that occurred in the era of Islam) that the heirs who are children from the father's side are equal in all ranks, then those from the mother's side will be more entitled and whoever is closer to the father will be more entitled to the property."
"3016","Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Alhad said: The freed slaves of Abu Hudhayfah: Salim died in the Battle of Yamamah and left two hundred dirhams as a legacy."
"3017","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Maternal brothers will inherit, paternal brothers will not inherit, and a man will inherit from his real brother except for his paternal brother (i.e., a paternal brother will not inherit in the presence of a real brother).\""
"3018","Nu'man bin Salim said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him: What is your opinion about the fact that a man dies leaving behind his grandson, will he be the heir of the deceased? Sayyiduna Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said: No (because the grandson is not an heir, even if he becomes an Asaba, he will not take the inheritance)."
"3019","Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: The mother is the assaba of one who has no other assaba, and the sister is the assaba of one who has no other assaba."
"3020","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Deliver the inheritance to its rightful owners, and whatever remains is the share of the nearest male (relative) (of the deceased).\""
"3021","It was narrated from Muhammad bin Ash'ath that his Jewish maternal grandmother died in Yemen, and he mentioned it to Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Whoever is his closest relative in his religion will be his heir. (That is, if you are a Muslim, you will not be the heir of this Jewish paternal grandmother, her Jewish relative will be her heir.)"
"3022","Tariq bin Shahab said: The maternal grandmother of Ash'ath bin Qays, who was a Jew, died, and he came to Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he replied: Those who follow his religion (i.e., Jews only) will be his heirs."
"3023","Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: We are not the heirs of the polytheists, nor will they be our heirs."
"3024","Sha'bi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Verily, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) did not consider people of two (different) religions as heirs."
"3025","Amir (al-Shaabi) may Allah have mercy on him said: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: People of two (different) nations will not inherit each other."
"3026","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"We will not be the heirs of the People of the Book, nor will they be our heirs. Except when a man's slave or his slave girl dies.\" (That is, a Muslim is not the heir of a non-Muslim, but if a non-Muslim slave or concubine dies, his property will be given to the master.)"
"3027","The translation of this hadith is the same as above."
"3028","Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyidna Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, considered a Muslim to be the heir of a disbeliever, but he did not consider a disbeliever to be the heir of a Muslim. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? He said: No (that is, inheritance between the two is not permissible as mentioned in the Sahih Hadith)."
"3029","Amir al-Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Mu'zala bint Harith died in Yemen, and Ash'ath bin Qays, whose paternal grandmother she was, came to Sayyiduna Umar to inquire about her inheritance."
"3030","Anas bin Sireen said: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: People of two different nations will not inherit, and whoever does not inherit will not be deprived."
"3031","On the authority of Sayyidina Usama bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A Muslim cannot inherit from a disbeliever, and neither can a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.\""
"3032","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When a man dies, the right of the heir (inheritance) becomes obligatory, and he did not keep anything from the inheritance for the one who was a Muslim or a free man before the distribution of the inheritance."
"3033","Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A Muslim cannot be the heir of an infidel, nor can an infidel be the heir of a Muslim.\""
"3034","The translation and recitation of this hadith is the same as above."
"3035","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: There is no legacy for the schools as long as there is an agreed amount to be paid on top of it."
"3036","It was narrated on the authority of Ata that about a man whose sons are slaves, some thirds and some fourths of them have been freed. Ata said: There will be no heirs (of the father) unless they are completely freed."
"3037","It was narrated from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, about the man who bought his son in his illness (death) and he has left one-third, then he (the son of the father) will be the heir, and if the property still remains to be determined, then he will not be the heir."
"3038","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: The limit of the schools is the limit of the Mamluk (i.e. the entire slave) until he is freed."
"3039","On the authority of Imam al-Zuhri, may God have mercy on him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The teacher is a brother in religion and a brother who frees, and the most entitled to his inheritance is the one who is closest to the freer.\" «Naemat» means «Saheb al-Manna»."
"3040","Muhammad bin Salim said: It was narrated on the authority of Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him: A person who freed a slave, then the freer (owner and master) and the slave died and the freer left his father and son, then the property will belong to the son."
"3041","Saeed bin Al-Musayyib, may God have mercy on him, said: It was narrated from Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him: If a man leaves his father and his grandson, then the inheritance will belong to the grandson."
"3042","Khasif narrated: It was narrated from Ziyad bin Abi Maryam that a woman freed her slave, then the woman died and left behind her son and brother, then her slave also died, so the son of the woman (the freed) and the brother of the woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for an inheritance. If he committed any sin, who would be responsible? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"You were responsible.\""
"3043","Al-Mughira said: I asked Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him: A man freed his slave, then the slave and the freedman died, and the freedman left the father and his son, so he said: This is for the father, and the child belongs to his son."
"3044","Narrated by Shu'ba: I heard from Hakam and Hamad, they used to say: (In the above case, the rightful owner of the property of the slave is only) that property belongs to the son."
"3045","It was narrated from Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Jannat al-Baqi and saw a man being sold. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him and bought him, then left him (i.e., did not buy him). Another man saw him and bought him and set him free. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"He is your (Islamic) brother and slave\", he asked what is your opinion about keeping him with you? He said: \"If he thanked you, it is better for him, and not good for you, and if he is ungrateful to you, it is better for you and bad for him.\" He asked: What is your opinion about his wealth? He said: \"If he dies and there are no heirs to collect the property, then you are his heir.\""
"3046","It was narrated from Abdullah bin Shaddad that the daughter of Sayyiduna Hamzah (RA) freed her slave, and that slave died leaving his daughter and Malika bint Hamzah, so the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) divided his inheritance half between his daughter and his mistress."
"3047","Shamus al-Kandiya said: I took a case to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that my father had left me and Malik (the freedman), so he gave half to me and the other half to the freedman Malik."
"3048","On the authority of Abul Knud, the case of a girl (daughter) and a master (owner) was brought to Sayyiduna Ali, and he gave half to the daughter and the other half to the liberating owner."
"3049","Narrated by Haqm bin Utaiba: Abd al-Rahman bin Mudalj died and left his daughter and the owners, Sayyiduna Ali gave half to the daughter and divided the other half among the owners."
"3050","It is narrated from Al-Shamus that when his father died, Sayyiduna Ali (RA) gave him half of the share and also gave half to the owners."
"3051","Jahm bin Dinar narrated that it was narrated from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, that he was asked: There are two sisters, one of them bought and freed his father, then he (the father) passed away, so Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: Two thirds for both sisters, as prescribed in the Holy Qur'an: . . . . .» [Al-Nisaa: 176/4] What remains will be for the liberating daughter only. That is, for the second sister, the remaining part will be none of the third and she will take the entire third."
"3052","It was narrated from Ash'a' that Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, narrated that the woman who freed her father, then the father died and left behind four daughters, one of whom was the freed one."
"3053","Hayan bin Salman said: I was with Suwayd bin Ghafla and a man came to him and asked about the share of the inheritance: A man left his daughter and his wife. He said: I am telling you the decision of Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him. He said: The decision of Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, is sufficient for me."
"3054","It was narrated from Abu al-Haytham that Ibrahim's concubine died and left a lot of property."
"3055","It was narrated on the authority of Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Ali, Sayyidna Zayd and I think Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with them) all said: Wala (inheritance) belongs to the elder and they used to mean the one who is closest to the father and mother."
"3056","Ubaidullah bin Utbah said: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) wrote to me about Faqeeh bint Samaan who died and left behind a son of a real brother and a son of a paternal brother."
"3057","It was narrated on the authority of Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them, both said: \"Walaa is for the elder\", and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, and (Qadi) Shareeh said: It will be for the heirs."
"3058","Sha'bi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Abdullah, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) decided the Wala for the eldest (heir)."
"3059","Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: Fakiha bint Samaan died and left a son of a paternal brother and a grandson of a real brother, so Sayyiduna Umar (RA) declared the sons of the paternal brother as heirs (because grandsons are guardians)."
"3060","It was narrated from Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him: Sayyiduna Umar, Sayyidna Ali, Sayyidna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) all said: Wala (inheritance) is for the elder."
"3061","It is narrated from al-Mughira that Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said about two brothers who inherited a slave who was freed by their father. One of the two brothers died and he left his son. Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sayyidna Ali, Sayyidna Zayd, Sayyidna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them) used to say: Wala is for the elder, that is, for the brother, nothing for the brother’s children."
"3062","Matar al-Waraq said: Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Wala is for the elder."
"3063","Taaws, may God have mercy on him, said: \"Wala'a is for the great.\""
"3064","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \"Walaa Haqq inheritance is for the elder.\""
"3065","On the authority of Yunus, Hasan, may God have mercy on him, narrated: A man who helps someone is among the Muslims, meaning that the Muslims will inherit him. Sufyan said: We also say the same."
"3066","Sayyiduna Tamim al-Dari, may God be pleased with him, says: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Messenger of God! What is the ruling if a person from among the disbelievers becomes a Muslim on the hand of a Muslim? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Whoever converts him to Islam is closer to him in both life and death.\""
"3067","On the authority of Mansoor, Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, was asked about the mixed people (Ahl al-Sadad) (where Muslims and non-Muslims are mixed), when one of them brought Islam at the hands of a Muslim? He said: He will give death on his behalf and the one who converts to Islam will be his heir."
"3068","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The wife will inherit the deed of the husband's murder."
"3069","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The rightful sharers of Dayat are the shares appointed by Allah."
"3070","Abu Qalaba said: The method of inheritance is like the method of inheritance."
"3071","Hameed and Dawud bin Abi Hind said: Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, wrote that the maternal brother should be made the inheritor of the inheritance."
"3072","Ibn Shihab said: The inheritance is between the heirs of the deceased according to the Book of Allah and its fixed shares."
"3073","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He who does not give inheritance to maternal brothers has committed injustice."
"3074","On the authority of Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Umar, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) said: The inheritance of inheritance will be divided in the same way as the inheritance of property is divided, whether the inheritance is due to murder or intentional murder."
"3075","Aamir (Shaabi) may Allah have mercy on him said: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to not give any inheritance to Akhiyafi brothers (i.e. maternal brothers), husbands and wives. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In some hadiths, a narrator is mentioned between Amir Shaabi and Ismail."
"3076","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Akhiafi's brother will not be the inheritor of Dayat."
"3077","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) said: All types of people will be heirs, but those whose death is caused by house collapse or drowning, they will not be heirs to each other, only living people will be their heirs."
"3078","Yahya bin Atiq said: I have read in some of the writings of Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him: Those on whom houses fell and it was not known who died first, and none of the deceased will be heirs to each other, but the heirs of the deceased will be the heirs."
"3079","Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to his father that Umm Kulthum and her son Zayd (Ibn Umar) both died on the same day, and they met those who wept for them on the way, none of them inherited their deceased, and the people of Hurrah did not inherit each other, and the people of Safin did not inherit each other."
"3080","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: A house in Syria fell upon some people whom Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, declared as heirs to each other."
"3081","Abu Harish said: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) declared the two brothers who died in the battle of Safin as heirs to each other."
"3082","It was narrated from Bakr bin Abdullah Muzni that a man died and left his paternal grandmother and his aunt."
"3083","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Whoever claimed kinship (closeness to mercy) will be given a share according to the closeness (kinship) to mercy."
"3084","Narrated Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, about a man who left his paternal grandmother and niece, he said: The niece will inherit the wealth."
"3085","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever has no heir, his maternal uncle is his heir.\""
"3086","Ibrahim (may God have mercy on him) said: The opinion of Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with them) was that the maternal uncle will be the heir."
"3087","It has been narrated from Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, about the paternal aunt and niece that all the wealth will belong to the niece."
"3088","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The wealth will be for the mother."
"3089","It has been narrated from Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, about the paternal aunt and niece that all the wealth will be for the brother's daughter."
"3090","Shaabi (may Allah have mercy on him) said about the niece and maternal aunt that I will give the wealth to the niece."
"3091","Narrated by Masrooq, may God have mercy on him: A man died and had no heirs except his niece and maternal uncle, he said: The maternal uncle has a share equal to that of the deceased's sister, and the niece has her father (i.e. the deceased's brother's share)."
"3092","It was narrated from Amir (Shaabi) that Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, used to place the paternal grandmother as the father in the absence of the father, and the aunt as the mother when there was no maternal uncle. That is, in the absence of parents, paternal grandmother and aunt used to give the father's and mother's share of inheritance."
"3093","It was narrated from Wasee bin Hibban that Ibn al-Dahdaha died and he used to come, that is, his loved ones and relatives were not known, he was from Bani Ajlan and there was no heir behind him. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Sayyiduna Asim bin Udi, may God be pleased with him: \"Do you know about his lineage in your tribe?\" He replied: O Messenger of Allah! We do not know him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called his nephew and gave him his entire inheritance."
"3094","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave property (inheritance) to his uncle."
"3095","Abu Hani said: Amir Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, was asked: A woman or a man died, and he left an aunt and a maternal grandmother, and there was no other heir or relative besides them. Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, used to give the aunt the share of the mother and the paternal grandmother the share of her brother, that is, the brother of the deceased woman."
"3096","On the authority of Hasan, may God have mercy on him, a man confessed at the time of his death that such and such a man had a thousand dirhams, another man proved with a binah (proof) that he also had a thousand dirhams, and the deceased left only a thousand dirhams? Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Half of the wealth should be divided between the two, unless the deceased is bankrupt, in which case it will not be permissible to accept his words."
"3097","Abu Na'im said: I asked the participant: What did you mention about the two brothers, one of whom claims to be (the deceased's) brother? He said: He will get his brother's share. I said: Who has mentioned this? He replied that Jabir told Amir and he told Sayyiduna Ali."
"3098","Narrated Amish (Sulaiman bin Mehran), Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: If some of the brothers claim to be (someone's) brother and others deny it, Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He will join the brothers as a slave, giving one of them a share in freeing. And Amir Wa Hakam and his disciples said: The brother who confessed will share from his share."
"3099","Wakiyyah, may God have mercy on him, said: One of the two brothers should claim to be the brother (of the third) and the other should deny it. He said: Ibn Abi Laila used to say: The issue will be six."
